`tests/suite/calc_test.go` (the specification — do not touch it) states the contract:

- `TestA` requires `calc.A() == 1`, otherwise it fails with `SHARED-FAILURE-EVIDENCE`.
- `TestB` requires `calc.B() == 2`, otherwise it fails with the same marker.

`services/calc/calc.go` currently returns `0` from both functions, so both assertions fail. The shared `SHARED-FAILURE-EVIDENCE` text in the harness output is why the two tests were grouped; it is a single root cause (stubbed return values in `calc`), not two unrelated bugs. Only `TestA`'s evidence was captured in the group output, but `TestB`'s assertion fails for the same reason and must be fixed in the same pass.

